<newsitem itemid="71464" id="root" date="1996-09-23" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Community Hospitals posts healthier profits.</title>
<headline>Community Hospitals posts healthier profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		21.8		   vs 17.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 10.0		   vs 8.8</p>
<p> Pretax		     10.7		   vs 8.5</p>
<p> Turnover		   69.6		   vs 63.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The UK's Community Hospitals Group Plc funds, develops, commissions and manages healthcare services.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 13.3		   vs 11.3</p>
<p> Interest payable	 2.66		   vs 2.74</p>
<p> Tax charge		 3.30		   vs 2.58</p>
<p> Net taxed		  7.36		   vs 5.96</p>
<p> Retained profit	  4.07		   vs 3.10</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 29</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 8</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 30</p>
<p>NOTE - The company, which said the current year had started well, noted that chairman Sir Peter Thompson, who will retire at the annual meeting, will be replaced by Alan Dexter. Robin Hodgson will become deputy chairman.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
